    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled in a tranquil country setting at Knock Cross, Balrothery, this beautifully maintained detached bungalow presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a substantial and highly appealing home on a generous c. 0.6-acre corner site. Combining a peaceful rural atmosphere with exceptional convenience, the property offers the best of both worlds, with Balrothery village and a host of amenities close by, while Dublin city and the surrounding motorway network are readily accessible.\nApproached by a private entrance, the property immediately impresses with its striking full redbrick façade, creating an attractive and timeless first impression while also offering the benefit of a low-maintenance exterior. Internally, the home has been lovingly maintained throughout and offers versatile accommodation currently arranged as a spacious three/four-bedroom bungalow, providing excellent flexibility for modern family living, those seeking additional reception or home-working space, or purchasers looking to downsize without compromising on space.\nA particular feature of this fine property is its wonderful private gardens. Set on a generous corner site, the grounds offer an enviable degree of privacy, with ample space for outdoor entertaining, gardening and family enjoyment. The mature setting and sense of space surrounding the house are rarely found so close to such a wide range of transport links and amenities. A detached garage with power further enhances the property's practicality, offering valuable storage, workshop or hobby space.\nThe location is exceptionally well connected. Situated just minutes' drive from Exit 5 of the M1 motorway, the property provides swift access to Dublin Airport, the M50 and the wider national road network. Balrothery village is close at hand, offering a range of everyday amenities and services, while the convenience of a bus stop just metres from the property provides a direct link towards Dublin city and Balbriggan Train Station, making commuting particularly straightforward.\nThe property is further complemented by double-glazed hardwood windows and oil-fired central heating, ensuring year-round comfort. With its distinctive redbrick exterior, generous site, private gardens, versatile accommodation and superb connectivity, Knock Cross represents a rare opportunity to acquire a characterful and exceptionally well-positioned country home within easy reach of Dublin.\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality, privacy and wonderful setting this unique property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.98m x 4.34m\nwith carpet flooring and large storage presses\n\nLiving Room - 4.93m x 4.23m\nwith wood flooring, feature fireplace with hardwood timber surround and marble hearth and backing, open fire behind the elect fire insert, sliding door to gardens\n\nDining / Sitting room - 4.5m x 4.56m\nwith wood flooring, french doors to rear\n\nKitchen - 4.2m x 3.47m\nwith tiled flooring and country style kitchen presses and worktop, plumbed for dishwasher and free standing cooker, door to utility room\n\nUtility Room - 1.98m x 2.7m\nwith tiled flooring, worktop and plumbed for washing machine, door to rear\n\nBathroom - 2.2m x 3.47\nlarge bathroom with bath and separate shower cubicle with pump shower, wc whb, fully tiled flooring and walls.\n\nBedroom One - 3.04m x 3.47m\nDouble room with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Two - 4.24m x 2.96m\nDouble room with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Three - 3.49m x 2.96m\nDouble room\n\nFamily room / fourth bedroom - 3.12m x 5.81m\nwith wood flooring, french doors to side, recessed lighting\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
